# KernelSU (KOWX712 fork) integrated-kernel support
# Source: CloudFox-Kernel drivers/kernelsu/kernel/Kconfig
#   https://github.com/CloudFox-INC/CloudFox-Kernel/blob/main/drivers/kernelsu/kernel/Kconfig
#
# CONFIG_KSU (tristate) has a KPROBES && EXT4_FS dependency:
#   - CONFIG_KPROBES for kernel hooking support
#   - CONFIG_EXT4_FS for `ext4_unregister_sysfs`
# Both are already =y in gki_defconfig; build-kernel.sh skips symbols already
# effective, so stating them here is idempotent and keeps the fragment
# self-contained (same pattern as zram-gki.config).
#
# The CloudFox kernel integration ships CONFIG_KSU default n ("This driver
# must stay disabled by default; ... Enabled builds opt in explicitly via
# make ... CONFIG_KSU=y"), so this fragment is the opt-in: =y compiles
# KernelSU into the kernel (integrated mode). The flashable zip therefore
# only needs to replace the kernel image on device (ksud `boot-patch
# --no-install`); no kernelsu.ko LKM and no ksuinit ramdisk component are
# involved.
#
# KSU_DEBUG, KSU_DISABLE_MANAGER and KSU_DISABLE_POLICY all default to n and
# are intentionally not pinned here.

CONFIG_KSU=y

# KSU Kconfig dependencies (already =y in gki_defconfig)
CONFIG_KPROBES=y
CONFIG_EXT4_FS=y
